# What Warlock is not about in this repository.
#
# gitignore syntax: a leading slash anchors to this directory, a trailing
# slash matches directories only.

# Prose about Warlock, not the code a document is written from.
/docs/

# Images and other binary content no summary is written from.
/assets/

/evals/

# Test modules. They used to sit inside the files they test, where
# `languages::elide` dropped them by their `#[cfg(test)]` block before any of
# them reached a pass. Split out under `#[path]` they are ordinary `.rs` files
# that no table recognises, so each would be sent whole — this file is where
# that is fixed, rather than by teaching warlock that a directory called
# `tests` is special in every repository it manages.
#
# It follows that a test-only edit no longer makes its directory stale, the
# same as an edit under `/docs/` above. That is the trade and it is the right
# way round: a document describes what the code does, and a rewritten
# assertion does not change that.
crates/*/src/tests/
